Repair and preserve the missing-value policy

safe_mean &lt;- function(x) {
  if (!is.numeric(x) || !is.null(dim(x))) {
    stop("x must be a numeric vector", call. = FALSE)
  }
  if (any(is.infinite(x))) {
    stop("x must not contain infinite values", call. = FALSE)
  }
  if (all(is.na(x))) return(NA_real_)
  mean(x, na.rm = TRUE)
}
safe_mean(c(2, NA, 4))

[1] 3


Keep Session 11’s contract: one numeric answer; numeric NA for empty or all-missing input; an error for invalid types, dimensions, or infinity.

Paired-input repair and evidence

paired_change &lt;- function(baseline, followup) {
  stopifnot(is.numeric(baseline), is.numeric(followup),
            is.null(dim(baseline)), is.null(dim(followup)))
  if (length(baseline) != length(followup)) {
    stop("paired inputs must have equal lengths", call. = FALSE)
  }
  if (any(is.infinite(baseline)) || any(is.infinite(followup))) {
    stop("paired inputs must not contain infinity", call. = FALSE)
  }
  followup - baseline
}
stopifnot(identical(paired_change(c(10, 20), c(8, 21)), c(-2, 1)))

Equal length is necessary. Matching patients and row order is still a separate precondition inherited from Session 11.

